msgid "Second-Order"
msgstr "Segundo orden"

msgid ""
"The model could not be estimated. Ensure that factors have at least 2 "
"observed variables."
msgstr ""
"No se pudo estimar el modelo. Asegúrese de que los factores tengan al menos "
"2 variables observadas."

msgid ""
"The model could not be estimated. A factor with less than 2 variables was "
"added in Second-Order."
msgstr ""
"No se pudo estimar el modelo. Se agregó un factor con menos de 2 variables "
"en el segundo orden."

msgid ""
"Not more cases than number of variables. Is your data a variance-covariance "
"matrix?"
msgstr ""
"No hay más casos que el número de variables. ¿Son sus datos una matriz de "
"varianzas-covarianzas?"

msgid "FIML missing data handling only available with ML-type estimators"
msgstr ""
"El manejo de datos ausentes de MVIC solo está disponible con estimadores de "
"tipo MV"

msgid ""
"Robust standard errors are not available with the GLS estimator. Try "
"changing the standard error method in the 'Advanced' settings to fit the "
"model."
msgstr ""
"No hay disponibles errores típicos robustos con el estimador MCG. Trata de "
"cambiar el método del error típico en las configuraciones 'Avanzadas' para "
"ajustar el modelo."

msgid ""
"Missing data handling '%s' is not supported for categorical data. \n"
" Please select another method under 'Missing data handling' within the "
"'Advanced' options tab"
msgstr ""
"El manejo de datos ausentes '%s' no se admite para datos con categorías. \n"
" Por favor, elige otro método en 'Manejo de datos ausentes' en la pestaña de "
"opciones 'Avanzadas'"

msgid ""
"The model could not be estimated. Error message: \n"
"\n"
" %s"
msgstr ""
"El modelo no se pudo estimar. Mensaje de error: \n"
"\n"
"%s"

msgid "The model is not admissible: %s"
msgstr "El modelo no es admisible: %s"

msgid "The model could not be estimated due to nonconvergence."
msgstr "El modelo no se pudo estimar debido a la no convergencia."

msgid "The model could not be estimated: No degrees of freedom left."
msgstr "No se pudo estimar el modelo: No quedan grados de libertad."

msgid "Bootstrapping is not available for variance-covariance matrix input."
msgstr ""
"El Bootstrapping no está disponible para la entrada de matrices de varianzas-"
"covarianzas."

msgid ""
"Robust standard errors are not available for variance-covariance matrix "
"input."
msgstr ""
"Los errores típicos robustos no están disponibles para una matriz de entrada "
"de varianzas-covarianzas."

msgid "# Factors"
msgstr "# Factores"

msgid "Model fit"
msgstr "Ajuste del modelo"

msgid ""
"Tests and measures of how well the factor model reproduces the observed data."
msgstr ""

msgid "Chi-square test"
msgstr "Contraste Chi-cuadrado"

msgid ""
"Chi-square test of the baseline model (the independence model) and of the "
"factor model. A non-significant p-value for the factor model indicates that "
"the model fits the data exactly, though this test is sensitive to sample "
"size. The footnote reports the estimator, the test statistic and the "
"standard error method that were used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model"
msgstr "Modelo"

msgid "df"
msgstr "gl"

msgid "p"
msgstr "p"

msgid "Baseline model"
msgstr "Modelo base"

msgid "Factor model"
msgstr "Modelo factorial"

msgid "%s You may consider changing the standard error method to 'robust'."
msgstr "%s Podrías pensar en cambiar el método del error típico a 'robusto'."

msgid ""
"%1$s The estimator is %2$s. The test statistic is %3$s. The standard error "
"method is %4$s."
msgstr ""
"%1$s El estimador es %2$s. El estadístico de prueba es %3$s. El método del "
"error típico es %4$s."

msgid "Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) test"
msgstr "Contraste de Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO)"

msgid ""
"Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin test of sampling adequacy. The measure of sampling "
"adequacy (MSA) is given for each indicator and overall, and for each group "
"in a multigroup analysis. Values closer to 1 indicate that the indicators "
"are well suited for factor analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bartlett's test of sphericity"
msgstr "Contraste de esfericidad de Bartlett"

msgid ""
"Bartlett's test of sphericity tests whether the correlation matrix of the "
"indicators is an identity matrix. A significant result means that the "
"correlation matrix is unlike the identity matrix, so that the indicators are "
"related."
msgstr ""

msgid "R-Squared"
msgstr "R-cuadrado"

msgid ""
"Proportion of variance in each indicator, and in each first-order factor if "
"a second-order factor is specified, that is explained by its predictors. "
"Values range from 0 to 1, with higher values indicating more variance "
"explained."
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional fit measures"
msgstr "Medidas de ajuste adicionales"

msgid ""
"Additional fit indices and information criteria for evaluating the overall "
"quality of the model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fit indices"
msgstr "Índices de ajuste"

msgid ""
"Incremental fit indices, which compare the factor model to the baseline "
"model. Common guidelines are CFI and TLI values above .95, but these should "
"be interpreted cautiously."
msgstr ""

msgid "Index"
msgstr "Índice"

msgid "Value"
msgstr "Valor"

msgid "Information criteria"
msgstr "Criterios de información"

msgid ""
"Log-likelihood, number of free parameters and information criteria (AIC, BIC "
"and the sample-size adjusted BIC). Lower values of the information criteria "
"indicate a better trade-off between fit and complexity when comparing models "
"fitted to the same data. They are only available with ML-type estimators."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other fit measures"
msgstr "Otras medidas de ajuste"

msgid ""
"Other fit measures: RMSEA with its 90%% confidence interval and the p-value "
"of the test of close fit, SRMR, Hoelter's critical N, GFI, MFI and ECVI. "
"Common guidelines are RMSEA below .06 and SRMR below .08, but these should "
"be interpreted cautiously."
msgstr ""

msgid "Metric"
msgstr "Métrica"

msgid "Log-likelihood"
msgstr "Log-verosimilitud"

msgid "Number of free parameters"
msgstr "Número de parámetros libres"

msgid "Akaike (AIC)"
msgstr "Criterio de Información de Akaike (AIC)"

msgid "Bayesian (BIC)"
msgstr "Bayesiano (BIC)"

msgid "Sample-size adjusted Bayesian (SSABIC)"
msgstr "Bayesiano ajustado por tamaño de muestra (SSABIC)"

msgid "Comparative Fit Index (CFI)"
msgstr "Índice de Ajuste Comparativo (CFI)"

msgid "Tucker-Lewis Index (TLI)"
msgstr "Índice de Tucker-Lewis (TLI)"

msgid "Bentler-Bonett Non-normed Fit Index (NNFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste no normalizado de Bentler-Bonett (NNFI)"

msgid "Bentler-Bonett Normed Fit Index (NFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste normalizado de Bentler-Bonett (NFI)"

msgid "Parsimony Normed Fit Index (PNFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste normalizado de parsimonia (PNFI)"

msgid "Bollen's Relative Fit Index (RFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste relativo de Bollen (RFI)"

msgid "Bollen's Incremental Fit Index (IFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste incremental de Bollen (IFI)"

msgid "Relative Noncentrality Index (RNI)"
msgstr "Índice de no centralidad relativa (RNI)"

msgid "Root mean square error of approximation (RMSEA)"
msgstr "Error cuadrático medio de aproximación (RMSEA)"

msgid "RMSEA 90%% CI lower bound"
msgstr "RMSEA 90 %% IC límite inferior"

msgid "RMSEA 90%% CI upper bound"
msgstr "RMSEA 90 %% IC límite superior"

msgid "RMSEA p-value"
msgstr "Valor P de RMSEA"

msgid "Standardized root mean square residual (SRMR)"
msgstr "Raíz del error cuadrado medio estandarizado (RECMS, SRMR)"

msgid "Hoelter's critical N (%s = .05)"
msgstr "N crítico de Hoelter (%s = .05)"

msgid "Hoelter's critical N (%s = .01)"
msgstr "N crítico de Hoelter (%s = .01)"

msgid "Goodness of fit index (GFI)"
msgstr "Índice de bondad de ajuste (GFI)"

msgid "McDonald fit index (MFI)"
msgstr "Índice de ajuste de McDonald (IMF)"

msgid "Expected cross validation index (ECVI)"
msgstr "Índice de validación cruzada esperado (ECVI)"

msgid ""
"Except for the PNFI, the fit indices are scaled because of categorical "
"variables in the data."
msgstr ""
"Excepto para el Índice PNFI, los índices se escalan a causa de las variables "
"con categorías en los datos."

msgid ""
"Except for the PNFI, the fit indices are scaled because a robust estimator "
"was used."
msgstr ""
"Excepto para el Índice PNFI, los índices se escalan a causa que se usó un "
"estimador robusto.."

msgid ""
"The RMSEA results are scaled because of categorical variables in the data."
msgstr ""
"Los resultados de la REACM (RMSEA) se escalan a causa de las variables con "
"categorías en los datos."

msgid "The RMSEA results are scaled because a robust estimator was used."
msgstr ""
"Los resultados de la REACM (RMSEA) se escalan a causa de que se usó un "
"estimador robusto."

msgid "Parameter estimates"
msgstr "Estimaciones de parámetros"

msgid ""
"Parameter estimates of the CFA model, organized by type: factor loadings, "
"factor variances and covariances, residual variances and covariances and, if "
"applicable, intercepts and thresholds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Not all bootstrap samples were successful: CI based on %.0f samples."
msgstr ""
"No fueron satisfactorias todas las muestras con bootstrap: IC basados en "
"%.0f muestras."

msgid "Std. estimate"
msgstr "Estimación tipificada"

msgid "Estimate"
msgstr "Estimar"

msgid "Factor loadings"
msgstr "Cargas de los factores"

msgid ""
"Factor loadings of the indicators on their factors. Each loading reflects "
"how strongly an indicator is related to its factor. With marker variable "
"identification, the loading of the first indicator of each factor is fixed "
"to 1."
msgstr ""

msgid "Group"
msgstr "Grupo"

msgid "Factor"
msgstr "Factor"

msgid "Indicator"
msgstr "Indicador"

msgid "Std. Error"
msgstr "Error típico"

msgid "z-value"
msgstr "Valor Z"

msgid "Lower"
msgstr "Inferior"

msgid "%s%% Confidence Interval"
msgstr "Intervalo con %s%% de confianza"

msgid "Upper"
msgstr "Superior"

msgid "Second-order factor loadings"
msgstr "Cargas factoriales de segundo orden"

msgid "Loadings of the first-order factors on the second-order factor."
msgstr ""

msgid "Factor variances"
msgstr "Varianzas de Factores"

msgid ""
"Estimated variances of the factors. They are fixed to 1 when the model is "
"identified by factor variances."
msgstr ""

msgid "Factor Covariances"
msgstr "Covarianzas de factores"

msgid "Estimated covariances between the factors."
msgstr ""

msgid "Residual variances"
msgstr "Varianzas de los errores"

msgid ""
"Residual variances of the indicators: the variance that is not explained by "
"the factors. Negative residual variances (Heywood cases) may indicate model "
"misspecification."
msgstr ""

msgid "Residual covariances"
msgstr "Covarianzas de los errores"

msgid ""
"Residual covariances between the pairs of indicators that were specified to "
"covary, i.e., shared variance that is not accounted for by the factors."
msgstr ""

msgid "Factor Intercepts"
msgstr "Constantes de los Factores"

msgid "Estimated intercepts (means) of the factors in each group."
msgstr ""

msgid "Intercepts"
msgstr "Constantes"

msgid "Estimated intercepts (means) of the indicators."
msgstr ""

msgid "Thresholds"
msgstr "Umbrales"

msgid ""
"Threshold parameters of the ordinal indicators. They define the cut-points "
"on the underlying continuous distribution that separate the observed "
"categories."
msgstr ""

msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "Umbral"

msgid "Modification Indices"
msgstr "Índices de Modificación"

msgid ""
"Modification indices (MI) estimate the expected decrease of the model chi-"
"square if a currently fixed parameter were freed. The expected parameter "
"change (EPC) indicates the approximate value of the freed parameter. Only "
"modification indices above the cutoff are shown."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-loadings"
msgstr "Cargas cruzadas"

msgid ""
"Modification indices for cross-loadings, i.e., loadings of indicators on "
"factors they are not assigned to."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mod. Ind."
msgstr "Mod. Ind."

msgid "EPC"
msgstr "CAP (EPC)"

msgid "Second-order cross-loadings"
msgstr "Cargas cruzadas de segundo orden"

msgid ""
"Modification indices for second-order cross-loadings, i.e., loadings of "
"first-order factors on second-order factors they are not assigned to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Modification indices for residual covariances between pairs of indicators."
msgstr ""

msgid "Modification indices"
msgstr "Índices de modificación"

msgid "No modification index was above the cutoff"
msgstr "Ningún índice de modificación está por encima del punto de corte"

msgid "Implied covariance matrices"
msgstr "Matrices de covarianza implícitas"

msgid "Implied covariance matrix"
msgstr "Matriz de covarianzas implícitas"

msgid ""
"Covariance matrix implied by the model, shown for each group in a multigroup "
"analysis. Close correspondence with the observed covariance matrix indicates "
"good model fit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Residual covariance matrices"
msgstr "Matrices de covarianzas de los errores"

msgid "Residual covariance matrix"
msgstr "Matriz de covarianzas de los errores"

msgid ""
"Difference between the observed and the model-implied covariance matrix, "
"shown for each group in a multigroup analysis. A perfect model shows all 0s; "
"small residuals indicate that the model reproduces the observed covariances "
"well."
msgstr ""

msgid "Plots"
msgstr "Gráficos"

msgid "Model plots"
msgstr "Gráficos de modelo"

msgid "Model plot"
msgstr "Gráfico del modelo"

msgid ""
"Graphical representation of the estimated model, showing the factors "
"(circles), the indicators (squares) and the paths between them. Shown for "
"each group in a multigroup analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Misfit plots"
msgstr "Gráficos desajustados"

msgid "Misfit plot"
msgstr "Gráfico desajustado"

msgid ""
"Residual correlations between the indicators, i.e., the correlations that "
"remain unexplained by the model. Larger values indicate pairs of indicators "
"that the model reproduces poorly. Shown for each group in a multigroup "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model syntax"
msgstr "Sintaxis del modelo"

msgid "The lavaan model syntax that corresponds to the specified model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Average variance extracted"
msgstr "Media de la varianza extraída"

msgid ""
"Average variance extracted (AVE): the amount of variance that is captured by "
"a factor relative to the amount of variance due to measurement error. Values "
"above .5 are commonly taken to indicate adequate convergent validity."
msgstr ""

msgid "AVE"
msgstr "VME (AVE)"

msgid "Heterotrait-monotrait ratio"
msgstr "Relación heterotraza-monotraza"

msgid ""
"Heterotrait-monotrait (HTMT) ratio of correlations for assessing "
"discriminant validity between the factors. Values clearly below 1 (more "
"conservatively, below .85 or .90) suggest that the factors are empirically "
"distinct."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reliability"
msgstr "Fiabilidad"

msgid ""
"Reliability of each factor and in total. Coefficient ω (omega) allows for "
"congeneric indicators (unequal loadings) and, with a second-order factor, is "
"also given for the second-order factor. Coefficient α (alpha) assumes tau-"
"equivalence (equal loadings). The total test score variance in the "
"denominator is the observed test score variance, i.e., the summed observed "
"covariance matrix. Values above .7 are commonly considered acceptable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coefficient %s"
msgstr "Coeficiente %s"

msgid "The reliability coefficients could not be computed: %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Column name %s already exists in the dataset"
msgstr "El nombre %s de columna ya existe en el conjunto de datos"

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the estimation of the polychoric/tetrachoric correlation "
"matrix failed. This is likely due to a small sample size. Internal error "
"message: %s"
msgstr ""
"Por desgracia, falló la estimación de la matriz de correlaciones policórica/"
"tetracórica. Esto es probable que se deba a un tamaño pequeño de la muestra. "
"Mensaje de fallo interno: %s"

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the estimation of the polychoric/tetrachoric correlation "
"matrix failed. This might be due to variable(s) %1$s not having the full "
"range of response categories. Internal error message: %2$s"
msgstr ""
"Por desgracia, falló la estimación de la matriz de correlaciones policórica/"
"tetracórica. Esto se puede deber a que la(s) variable(s) %1$s no contiene(n) "
"todas las categorías de respuesta. Mensaje de fallo interno: %2$s"

msgid "Estimation failed. Internal error message: %1$s. %2$s"
msgstr "La estimación falló. Mensaje de fallo interno: %1$s. %2$s"

msgid "Estimation failed. Internal error message: %s"
msgstr "La estimación falló. Mensaje de error interno: %s"

